<title>USA: Schwab sees US growth funds flow up in Sept.</title>
<headline>Schwab sees US growth funds flow up in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Charles Schwab Corp said cash flow into domestic growth mutual funds rose to $1.04 billion in September versus $752.2 million in August.</p>
<p>Cash into international growth funds fell to $174.3 million from $254.1 million, while balanced funds rose to $209 million from $128 million.</p>
<p>Taxable bond funds fell to $90.5 million from $210.6 million.</p>
<p>Tax-free bond funds had an outflow of $8.1 million in September versus an inflow of $60.9 million in August.</p>
</text>
